{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-87hc-h4r5-73f7","cve_id":"CVE-2026-21860","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-87hc-h4r5-73f7","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-87hc-h4r5-73f7","summary":" Werkzeug safe_join() allows Windows special device names with compound extensions","description":"Werkzeug's `safe_join` function allows path segments with Windows device names that have file extensions or trailing spaces. On Windows, there are special device names such as `CON`, `AUX`, etc that are implicitly present and readable in every directory. Windows still accepts them with any file extension, such as `CON.txt`, or trailing spaces such as `CON `.\n\nThis was previously reported as https://github.com/pallets/werkzeug/security/advisories/GHSA-hgf8-39gv-g3f2, but the fix failed to account for compound extensions such as `CON.txt.html` or trailing spaces. It also missed some additional special names.\n\n`send_from_directory` uses `safe_join` to safely serve files at user-specified paths under a directory. If the application is running on Windows, and the requested path ends with a special device name, the file will be opened successfully, but reading will hang indefinitely.","type":"reviewed","severity":"medium","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/werkzeug/security-advisories/GHSA-87hc-h4r5-73f7","source_code_location":"https://github.com/pallets/werkzeug","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-87hc-h4r5-73f7","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-21860","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/pallets/werkzeug/security/advisories/GHSA-87hc-h4r5-73f7","https://github.com/pallets/werkzeug/commit/7ae1d254e04a0c33e241ac1cca4783ce6c875ca3","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-21860","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-87hc-h4r5-73f7"],"published_at":"2026-01-08T19:51:21Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T19:57:32Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-01-08T19:51:21Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-01-08T19:15:59Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"Werkzeug"},"vulnerable_version_range":"< 3.1.5","first_patched_version":"3.1.5","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L","score":5.3},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","score":6.3}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-67","name":"Improper Handling of Windows Device Names"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login":"yueyueL","id":64764840,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NzY0ODQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64764840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yueyueL","html_url":"https://github.com/yueyueL","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yueyueL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yueyueL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yueyueL/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yueyueL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yueyueL/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yueyueL/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yueyueL/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yueyueL/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yueyueL/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"reporter"},{"user":{"login":"MushroomWasp","id":149011900,"node_id":"U_kgDOCOG9vA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149011900?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MushroomWasp","html_url":"https://github.com/MushroomWasp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MushroomWasp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MushroomWasp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MushroomWasp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MushroomWasp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mushroo